  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "What is the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2}=16$ and the plane $x=2$ onto the $yz$-plane.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the sphere and the plane $x=2$, we substitute $x=2$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 4+(y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =12 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $yz$-plane gives us the circle of radius $2\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-4,0).$",
